  "note": "createPurchaseService gains the passive nativePaymentLaneRead({operationId,token,key}) and createProtocolPurchases the passive readRetainedNativePaymentLane(operation,key); both are on the public passive lists, so they run while purchase actions are held or the host is stopped and never read the stop check. After the one-time wallet guard was issued, they re-read the approval, coordinates, handoff and guard events, retained Agreement receipt and seller commitment from the local stores (src/dacs/retained-native-lane-proof.mjs), read the one retained lane record, and read every row and event again after it; they resolve {readback:true,retained:{stage,hash,nonce}} and reject native_payment_lane_held, native_payment_lane_unverified, network_identity_mismatch, wallet_lane_mismatch or wallet_fenced, with no recheck, lock or save. A native payment_handoff event now records sellerCommitmentWitness, the digest of the saved seller commitment. purchaseCommitment and COMMITMENT_DOMAIN moved to the new module unchanged and are re-exported from purchases.mjs."
}
